The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=18$) is the interval between $x=16$ and $x=19$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
g'(18)&\approx\dfrac{g(19)-g(16)}{19-16}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{96-87}{3}
\\\\
&=3
\end{align}$
